{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>From your midst.</b> From your midst, and the meaning concerns thought. Or מתוכך means from among Israel. And the meaning of תָּטֶה is to incline." "<b>Send the finger.</b> A verbal noun on the pattern of כִּשְׁכַּב אֲדֹנִי הַמֶּלֶךְ (1 Kings 1:25), as if he said to send a hand to strike his fellow, or to take his wealth. Also וְדִבֵּר אָוֶן is a verbal noun."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:08.665606513Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}